index 28d3e9b4..9fffd909 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -241,8 +241,15 @@ Namespace changes validate types, capacity and replacement before mutation.
 Relative AT_FDCWD paths follow the calling process's image cwd; owned directory
 FDs resolve relative operations through their current VFS identity. Image chdir,
 getcwd and relative image exec retain native per-process cwd semantics. Entering
-owned directories as cwd, relative image-directory FD access, owned symlinks,
-hardlinks and guest file mappings remain unsupported.
+owned directories as cwd, relative image-directory FD access, hardlinks and
+guest file mappings remain unsupported.
+Owned symlink/symlinkat and readlink/readlinkat support bounded targets and
+nofollow metadata. Link expansion precedes later parent components; mutations
+name the final link itself, including directory requirements on trailing slashes.
+Exclusive create and O_NOFOLLOW keep their separate failure behavior. Owned links
+resolve within assigned storage; entering the native image through an owned link
+remains unsupported. Image aliases into storage retain assignment precedence.
+Link target bytes consume the same owned storage capacity as regular data.
 Component-wise image-link traversal preserves assignment
 precedence, missing components and non-directory errors. Native image operations
 use a temporary canonical path below the stopped workload's stack; an unavailable
